    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_title">Shelf %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_what">Scan a book\'s barcode and it finds the book\'s call number, then lists the whole collection in shelf order.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_heading">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_lookups">To look a book up, Shelf sends its ISBN or LCCN, or the title and author you search for, to the Library of Congress catalogue (lx2.loc.gov) and to Open Library (openlibrary.org). The Library of Congress answers only over plain HTTP, so what goes to it is not encrypted. Nothing else about you or your books goes with it, and neither needs an account.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_cloud">If you sign in to Nextcloud, the catalogue and a spreadsheet of the shelf order sync with the folder you choose on that server, and with every phone signed in to it; while Shelf is open it checks that folder every 15 seconds for books another phone added. Your sign-in details are kept on this phone. Nothing is sent to the app\'s maker.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_phone">The camera reads barcodes, printed ISBNs and Nextcloud\'s sign-in code on the phone; no picture is kept or sent. If Audiobooks is installed, a book\'s page asks it, on the phone, whether it has that book. There are no ads, no analytics and no tracking. Spreadsheets you save go only where you choose to save them.</string>
    <string name="about_terms_heading">Terms</string>
    <string name="about_terms">This app is free software under the GNU General Public License v3. It comes with no warranty: use it at your own risk. Call numbers come from the catalogues and can be wrong.</string>
    <string name="about_open_source_heading">Open source</string>
    <string name="about_bundled">Built with Mudita MMD, AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, CameraX, OkHttp and Kotlin; barcodes are read with zxing-cpp and printed numbers with Tesseract (with Leptonica, libjpeg and libpng) and its English model; the Lato typeface and Material Symbols icons. The full list, with each licence and its text, is under Licences.</string>
